{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for observability Draft2 exact4f0057acc452ad0f7ec59356ac17ba65d55ee671.\n\nThe five Draft1 boundaries are materially improved: no raw tracestate, distinct server request ID, operational admin-only sidecar, actual paged status reads/minimal readiness RPC, and weighted version-filtered gate with no-data/freshness checks. Prospective behavior is not implementation proof. Remaining corrections:\n\n[P2] Close the metric schema over its own legitimate events (§4.2–4.3). Blob4 permits route names but rows require alarm, dispatch, metrics, fixed diagnosis steps and none. Blob6 permits native reason enums but route/drop rows require2xx–5xx and budget/tainted. Faithful validation drops ordinary events and its fallback; specify a valid nonrecursive fallback and exact per-kind unions. Hosted tools-list/tool-call/custody also need allowed kinds and slots or a separately versioned map. Preserve all promised fields, distinguish actual End.answer from idle, and give numeric ranges/count semantics. W1 should cover every legitimate/fallback row, not only tainted examples.\n\n[P2] Make critical-event coverage compatible with the hard budget (§4.2,4.7). Sixteen/request or32/alarm plus a terminal drop summary exceeds the stated cap unless a slot is reserved. Native dispatcher can process many due duties and each give-up runs a turn: prioritizing turn cannot prove every turn survives. Specify buffering/aggregation/reservations and explicit critical-loss coverage with overflow witnesses that leave native effects unchanged. An observed no-busy gate must not silently pass after relevant events were dropped. Weight counter values as well as event rows; define operational error taxonomy/denominator and verify health response's expected deployment/version, not merely HTTP200.\n\n[P2] Readiness must mean active, valid register (§4.6). Exists-and-not-provisional includes refused genesis: native Status is provisional|active|refused. Require active register state and witness refused/nonregister as503. Specify deterministic configured selector/ambiguity. A cached result alone allows concurrent cold misses; retain a shared in-flight probe and test concurrent polling for the claimed one-probe/5s bound. A timeout is an observational limit, not proof that the underlying RPC stopped. The minimal non-data probe and real sessionsOf validation otherwise repair the earlier authority problem.\n\n[P2] Isolate sidecar storage and state retained-window coverage (§4.4–4.5,7). Sink fault witnesses do not cover SQL faults at entry/duty boundaries. Define best-effort sidecar writes outside native success decisions; failure/slowdown/restart/overflow must not roll back, resubmit or replace accepted entries/sends. Add those witnesses. A4096-row ring that replaces older-than-seven-day rows first does not expire idle old rows. Define actual age policy, validated bounded filters/pages/cursors and eviction/retention coverage; complete means the retained window, not proof of historical absence or settlement. Preserve each page/column's observed heads and moving/partial counts, rather than a single invented snapshot. Operational context propagation must leave native messages/types untouched.\n\n[P2] Finish trace validation and qualify privacy claims (§4.4). Validate exact lowercase version00 framing, nonzero trace AND parent IDs, and outgoing supported flags; ignore invalid context without logging it. Add zero-parent/extra-suffix/length witnesses. W3C marks an all-zero parent invalid. [Trace Context](https://www.w3.org/TR/trace-context/). Exact hex shape cannot prove a caller-selected ID contains no encoded secret: call it untrusted correlation, preserve admin/access/retention boundaries and disclose collision/linking limits. This requires no semantic secret detector or rejection of all adopted trace IDs. Distinguish native answer-body equality from intentionally added HTTP headers.\n\nArchitecture: operational correlation and native read reuse are sound after schema, readiness and coverage corrections. Security: raw vendor text removal and authority separation pass; sidecar isolation and truthful untrusted-ID boundaries remain. Simplification: keep one typed sink and minimal probe, with explicit invariants rather than contradictory special cases. Full scope remains; estimates sequence it.\n\nValidation:24657B primary FULL Root/peers,34017B U3 FULL peers; both finals/three audits FULL Root. Native inherited blobs, new selected Source fragments/host module and contiguous unit metadata verified against013fac. No whole Source survey/private woo claim. Root audit588B SHA5b1528583bc19789144c4b16a1cb6eb57c794074d5fe8f1df36a272ed0117e8c. Source status also independently read at Root. W1–W3/calibration remain prospective and UNRUN. No Source execution/tests/gate/install/provider/browser/private reads; no contract amendment, implementation, deployment or parent acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:065260027bfbfcdf5f18505ecca31b96aee1acf7","binding":"assigned","head":"4f0057acc452ad0f7ec59356ac17ba65d55ee671","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:292108a95ada0c4f07cafde22cb4031ab340dc21\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6264f1e8e28666333a7c9564e5cb74a347b33a7c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:136712b9cf9ce6a67cb2d2ee1dd9a567c6945a43","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}